IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VI: "Investigations" (s 124) and the first half of "Enforcement" (s 125:
-- information or complaint, limitation of prosecutions, and proof by certificate and affidavit). Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. In addition:
--   * A provision on evidence is a BOOLEAN that is TRUE when the document has the effect the text gives it
--     ("is evidence of", "is conclusive proof of", "is deemed to be"). FALSE means this section does not give it that effect.
--   * "Other than Part IV" is carried as a BOOLEAN input where the text says it, because Part IV (piece ei3) has its own enforcement rules.
--   * What an affidavit "states" is a fact about the affidavit, not about the world: the text makes the statement itself the evidence.
-- Hohfeld, for s 125: the Commission's power to prove by certificate or affidavit is the accused's liability to have it so proved;
-- the accused's limitation immunity (s 125(4)) is the Commission's disability to prosecute after five years.

§ `Part VI -- Investigations`

§§ `s 124 Investigation by Commission`

-- Subsections (1), (2) and (4) are machinery and are not encoded (see the coverage table): the Governor in Council's direction,
-- the Commission's Inquiries Act powers, and the Minister's duty to lay a report before Parliament. Subsection (3) gives the public a claim.
-- src:1844 | (3) The Commission shall give such public notice as it considers sufficient of its intention to investigate any matters that under this Act it is empowered to investigate, and it shall receive representations submitted to it by persons or associations of persons appearing to the Commission to have an interest in the matters under investigation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 124(3) (src:1844)
GIVEN `the matter is one that under this Act the Commission is empowered to investigate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission intends to investigate the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 124(3) the Commission must give public notice of its intention to investigate the matter` IF
        `the matter is one that under this Act the Commission is empowered to investigate`
    AND `the Commission intends to investigate the matter`

-- The person's claim: a person or association "appearing to the Commission to have an interest" is a judgment of the Commission, so an input.
-- src:1844 | (3) The Commission shall give such public notice as it considers sufficient of its intention to investigate any matters that under this Act it is empowered to investigate, and it shall receive representations submitted to it by persons or associations of persons appearing to the Commission to have an interest in the matters under investigation.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 124(3) (src:1844)
GIVEN `the matter is under investigation by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or association appears to the Commission to have an interest in the matters under investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or association has submitted representations to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` IF
        `the matter is under investigation by the Commission`
    AND `the person or association appears to the Commission to have an interest in the matters under investigation`
    AND `the person or association has submitted representations to the Commission`

§ `Part VI -- Enforcement`

§§ `s 125(1) to (4) Information or complaint, two or more offences, territorial jurisdiction, limitation of prosecutions`

-- Who may lay an information or complaint. The text says "may", so it is a permission given to two kinds of person; it does not
-- say that no one else may (fork F-ei4-8).
-- src:1850 | 125 (1) An information or complaint under this Act, other than Part IV, may be laid or made by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by a person acting for the Commission and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act, other than Part IV, it is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(1) (src:1850)
GIVEN `the information or complaint is under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(1) an information or complaint may be laid or made by the person` IF
        `the information or complaint is under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND (`is a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` OR `is a person acting for the Commission`)

-- src:1850 | 125 (1) An information or complaint under this Act, other than Part IV, may be laid or made by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by a person acting for the Commission and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act, other than Part IV, it is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(1) (src:1850)
GIVEN `the information or complaint is under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(1) the information or complaint is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission` IF
        `the information or complaint is under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `the information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act`

-- Only the Commission, a person acting for it, or a person acting for Her Majesty may call the authority into question.
-- src:1850 | 125 (1) An information or complaint under this Act, other than Part IV, may be laid or made by a member of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police or by a person acting for the Commission and, if an information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act, other than Part IV, it is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission and shall not be called into question for lack of authority of the informant or complainant except by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(1) (src:1850)
GIVEN `the information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person acting for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(1) the person may call into question the authority of the informant or complainant` IF
        `the information or complaint appears to have been laid or made under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND (   `the person is the Commission`
         OR `the person is a person acting for the Commission`
         OR `the person is a person acting for Her Majesty`)

-- TRUE means the objection is barred: no proceeding is objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences.
-- src:1852 | (2) An information or complaint about an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, may be for one or more offences and no information, complaint, warrant, conviction or other proceeding in a prosecution under this Act, other than Part IV, is objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(2) (src:1852)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in a prosecution under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding relates to two or more offences` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(2) the proceeding is not objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences` IF
        `the proceeding is in a prosecution under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `the proceeding relates to two or more offences`

-- src:1854 | (3) An information or complaint about an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, may be heard, tried or determined by any provincial court judge, as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, if the accused is resident, carrying on business, found, apprehended or in custody within the judge’s territorial jurisdiction although the matter of the information or complaint did not arise within that jurisdiction.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(3) (src:1854)
GIVEN `the information or complaint is about an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a provincial court judge as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is carrying on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` IF
        `the information or complaint is about an offence under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `is a provincial court judge as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code`
    AND (   `the accused is resident within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
         OR `the accused is carrying on business within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
         OR `the accused is found within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
         OR `the accused is apprehended within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`
         OR `the accused is in custody within the judge's territorial jurisdiction`)

-- Limitation of prosecutions. Read as a limit: after the last day below a prosecution may not be commenced (fork F-ei4-7). For an
-- offence under Part IV this subsection does not speak, so the answer is NOTHING, not a date and not FALSE.
-- src:1856 | (4) A prosecution for an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, may be commenced at any time within five years after the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(4) (src:1856)
GIVEN `the offence is under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` IS
    IF `the offence is under Part IV`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`add years` `the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` 5)

-- src:1856 | (4) A prosecution for an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, may be commenced at any time within five years after the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(4) (src:1856)
GIVEN `the offence is under Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the prosecution is commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` IS
    CONSIDER `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` `the offence is under Part IV` `the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastday THEN JUST (`the day on which the prosecution is commenced` AT MOST lastday)

§§ `s 125(5) Certificate`

-- The certificate is "conclusive proof" of the day the Commission became aware, which is the day s 125(4) counts from.
-- The text does not repeat "other than Part IV" in this subsection.
-- src:1858 | (5) A document appearing to have been issued by the Commission, certifying the day on which it became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution, is admissible in evidence and shall be considered conclusive proof of that fact without proof of the signature or the official character of the person appearing to have signed the document and without any other proof.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(5) (src:1858)
GIVEN `the document appears to have been issued by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document certifies the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(5) the document is admissible in evidence and is conclusive proof of the day on which the Commission became aware` IF
        `the document appears to have been issued by the Commission`
    AND `the document certifies the day on which the Commission became aware of the subject-matter of the prosecution`

§§ `s 125(6) to (10) Affidavits of a person acting for the Commission`

-- The affidavit itself. "affidavit" is the s 2(1) definition in the keel (sworn or affirmed before a commissioner of oaths or another
-- person authorized to take affidavits); the affiant must be a person acting for the Commission.
-- src:1860 | (6) If provision is made by this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations for personal service of a request for information, notice or demand, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(6) to (9) (src:1860)
DECLARE `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` HAS
    `sworn or affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1860 | (6) If provision is made by this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations for personal service of a request for information, notice or demand, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(6) to (9) (src:1860)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` IF
        `s 2(1) affidavit` (affidavit's `sworn or affirmed`) (affidavit's `before a commissioner of oaths`) (affidavit's `before any other person authorized to take affidavits`)
    AND affidavit's `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission`

-- src:1860 | (6) If provision is made by this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations for personal service of a request for information, notice or demand, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that
-- src:1861 | (a) the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case,
-- src:1862 | (b) such a request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed, and
-- src:1863 | (c) the person identifies as an exhibit attached to the affidavit a true copy of the request, notice or demand,
-- src:1864 | is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(6) (src:1860-1864)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
      `provision is made by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations for personal service of the request for information, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit identifies as an exhibit attached to it a true copy of the request, notice or demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` IF
        `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` affidavit
    AND `provision is made by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations for personal service of the request for information, notice or demand`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
    AND `the affidavit states that the request, notice or demand was served personally on a named day on the person to whom it was directed`
    AND `the affidavit identifies as an exhibit attached to it a true copy of the request, notice or demand`

-- src:1866 | (7) If a person is required by this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that the person
-- src:1867 | (a) has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1868 | (b) after a careful examination and search of the records, has been unable to find in a given case that the return, statement, answer or certificate, as the case may be, has been filed or made by the person required to do so,
-- src:1869 | is evidence that in that case the person did not do so.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(7) (src:1866-1869)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
      `the person is required by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that after a careful examination and search of the records the person has been unable to find in a given case that the return, statement, answer or certificate has been filed or made by the person required to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(7) the affidavit is evidence that in that case the person did not file or make the return, statement, answer or certificate` IF
        `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` affidavit
    AND `the person is required by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `the affidavit states that after a careful examination and search of the records the person has been unable to find in a given case that the return, statement, answer or certificate has been filed or made by the person required to do so`

-- src:1871 | (8) If a person is required by this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that the person
-- src:1872 | (a) has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1873 | (b) after careful examination of the records, has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day,
-- src:1874 | is evidence that it was filed or made on that day and not before.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(8) (src:1871-1874)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
      `the person is required by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that after careful examination of the records the person has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(8) the affidavit is evidence that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on that day and not before` IF
        `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` affidavit
    AND `the person is required by this Act other than Part IV or the regulations to make a return, statement, answer or certificate`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `the affidavit states that after careful examination of the records the person has found that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on a particular day`

-- src:1876 | (9) An affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that
-- src:1877 | (a) the person has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1878 | (b) a document annexed to the affidavit is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Commission or a person acting for the Commission,
-- src:1879 | is evidence of the nature and contents of the document and is admissible in evidence and has the same probative force as the original document would have if it were proven in the ordinary way.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(9) (src:1876-1879)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that a document annexed to it is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Commission or a person acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(9) the affidavit is evidence of the nature and contents of the document and is admissible with the same probative force as the original` IF
        `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` affidavit
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `the affidavit states that a document annexed to it is a document or true copy of a document made by or for an employer, the Commission or a person acting for the Commission`

-- src:1881 | (10) If evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making the affidavit is acting for the Commission, it is not necessary to prove
-- src:1882 | (a) the person’s signature;
-- src:1883 | (b) that the person is acting for the Commission; or
-- src:1884 | (c) the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(10) (src:1881-1884)
GIVEN `evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making the affidavit is acting for the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(10) it is not necessary to prove the signature, that the person is acting for the Commission, or the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn` IF
    `evidence is offered under this section by an affidavit from which it appears that the person making the affidavit is acting for the Commission`

§§ `s 125(11) to (14) Judicial notice, deemed documents and forms, proof of return`

-- src:1886 | (11) Judicial notice shall be taken of all orders made under this Act, other than Part IV, without the orders being specially pleaded or proven.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(11) (src:1886)
GIVEN `the order is made under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(11) judicial notice shall be taken of the order without its being specially pleaded or proven` IF
    `the order is made under this Act other than Part IV`

-- src:1888 | (12) Every document appearing to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision or other document executed under, or in the course of, the administration or enforcement of this Act, other than Part IV, over the name in writing of the Commission, or a person acting for the Commission under this Act, other than Part IV, is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Commission or the person unless it has been called into question by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(12) (src:1888)
GIVEN `the document appears to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is executed under, or in the course of, the administration or enforcement of this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is over the name in writing of the Commission or of a person acting for the Commission under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document has been called into question by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(12) the document is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Commission or the person` IF
        `the document appears to be an order, direction, demand, notice, certificate, requirement, decision or other document`
    AND `the document is executed under, or in the course of, the administration or enforcement of this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `the document is over the name in writing of the Commission or of a person acting for the Commission under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND NOT (`the document has been called into question by the Commission or by a person acting for it or for Her Majesty`)

-- src:1890 | (13) A form that appears to be authorized by the Commission is deemed to be a form authorized by the Commission under this Act, other than Part IV, unless called into question by the Commission or a person acting for it or for Her Majesty.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(13) (src:1890)
GIVEN `the form appears to be authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form has been called into question by the Commission or a person acting for it or for Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(13) the form is deemed to be a form authorized by the Commission under this Act other than Part IV` IF
        `the form appears to be authorized by the Commission`
    AND NOT (`the form has been called into question by the Commission or a person acting for it or for Her Majesty`)

-- Proof "in the absence of evidence to the contrary": a rebuttable presumption, so the contrary evidence is an input.
-- src:1892 | (14) In a prosecution for an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, the production of a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under this Act, other than Part IV, or the regulations appearing to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged with the offence or to have been made or signed by or for the person is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the return, certificate, statement or answer was filed or delivered by or for that person or was made or signed by or for them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(14) (src:1892)
GIVEN `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under this Act other than Part IV or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document appears to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged with the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document appears to have been made or signed by or for the person charged with the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` IF
        `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `the document is a return, certificate, statement or answer required by or under this Act other than Part IV or the regulations`
    AND (   `the document appears to have been filed or delivered by or for the person charged with the offence`
         OR `the document appears to have been made or signed by or for the person charged with the offence`)
    AND NOT (`there is evidence to the contrary`)

