§§ `s 125(16) Proof of records`

-- Subsection (16) says "a prosecution for an offence under this Act" with no "other than Part IV" (subsections (5), (9) and (10) do not
-- say it either; the rest of s 125 does).
-- src:1895 | (16) In a prosecution for an offence under this Act, an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission stating that
-- src:1896 | (a) the person has charge of the appropriate records, and
-- src:1897 | (b) an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of fines, penalties, interest and repayment of overpayments of benefits has not been received by the Receiver General,
-- src:1898 | is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(16) (src:1895-1898)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission`
      `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of fines, penalties, interest and repayment of overpayments of benefits has not been received by the Receiver General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(16) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` IF
        `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` affidavit
    AND `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under this Act`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person has charge of the appropriate records`
    AND `the affidavit states that an examination of the records shows that an amount required under this Act to be remitted to the Receiver General on account of fines, penalties, interest and repayment of overpayments of benefits has not been received by the Receiver General`

§§ `s 125(17) Officers, etc., of corporations`

-- The officer, director or agent is a party to the offence and liable to the punishment "whether or not the corporation has been
-- prosecuted or convicted", so whether the corporation has been prosecuted is not an input.
-- src:1900 | (17) If a corporation commits an offence under this Act, other than Part IV, any officer, director or agent of the corporation who directed, authorized, assented to, acquiesced in or participated in the commission of the offence is a party to and guilty of the offence and is liable on conviction to the punishment provided for the offence whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 125(17) (src:1900)
GIVEN `a corporation commits an offence under this Act other than Part IV` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an officer, director or agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `directed the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorized the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assented to the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participated in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` IF
        `a corporation commits an offence under this Act other than Part IV`
    AND `is an officer, director or agent of the corporation`
    AND (   `directed the commission of the offence`
         OR `authorized the commission of the offence`
         OR `assented to the commission of the offence`
         OR `acquiesced in the commission of the offence`
         OR `participated in the commission of the offence`)
